# `data/manifest.json` pins the SHA-256 of every byte under `data/`, and
# `core.autocrlf` is true in this repo: without this line a fresh Windows
# checkout would materialise CRLF and `verify` would fail on a clean clone.
# `-text` (not `eol=lf`) because the files are copies whose bytes must match
# their sources exactly, whatever line endings those carry. It lives beside
# `data/`, not in it, because `prepare` rebuilds `data/` from scratch.
data/** -text
